{"title":"Career Roadmap · Data Analyst","role":"Data Analyst","summary":"A Data Analyst transforms raw data into useful information for business, scientific, financial, operational, and strategic decisions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Mathematics"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Data Analyst transforms raw data into useful information for business, scientific, financial, operational, and strategic decisions."},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc. Mathematics graduate has a particularly strong foundation for analytics because the degree develops:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mathematical reasoning"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Logical problem-solving"},{"text":"Quantitative modelling"},{"text":"The main gap is usually applied data and business technology rather than mathematical ability."}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mathematics","Statistics","SQL","Python","Excel","Power BI","Business Analytics"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A Mathematics graduate can eventually specialize in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Business analytics"},{"text":"Product analytics"},{"text":"Financial analytics"},{"text":"Risk analytics"},{"text":"Operations analytics"},{"text":"Marketing analytics"},{"text":"Quantitative analytics"},{"text":"Data science"},{"text":"Statistical modelling"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Sc. Mathematics"},{"text":"Mathematics + statistics + programming + analytics"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Data Analyst / BI Analyst"},{"text":"SQL, Python, Excel, dashboards"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior Data Analyst / Analytics Specialist"},{"text":"Advanced statistics, experimentation, modelling"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Analytics Lead / Data Strategy Professional"},{"text":"Analytics leadership and decision systems"}]]}]},{"heading":"Build the Mathematics Foundation","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Do not abandon mathematics simply because the target role is Data Analyst."},{"text":"Instead, convert mathematical knowledge into applied analytics capability."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Core mathematics"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Numerical methods"},{"text":"Discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Mathematical modelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Particularly important"},{"type":"p","text":"For Data Analytics, prioritize:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Probability","Statistics","Linear Algebra","Optimization"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Mathematics + Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Build the quantitative foundation."},{"type":"h","text":"Probability"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Random variables"},{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Conditional probability"},{"text":"Bayes' theorem"},{"text":"Expected value"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Covariance"},{"text":"Independence"},{"text":"Sampling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mean"},{"text":"Median"},{"text":"Variance"},{"text":"Standard deviation"},{"text":"Percentiles"},{"text":"Distributions"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Regression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematical Thinking → Data Analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"The transition should look like:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mathematical Problem","Define Variables","Build Model","Obtain Data","Statistical Analysis","Validate Assumptions","Interpret Results","Decision"]},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"The goal is not to perform mathematics for its own sake."},{"text":"The goal is to use mathematics to understand real-world data."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1–2 — Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Excel is one of the most useful tools for an entry-level analyst."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Sorting/filtering"},{"text":"IF/IFS"},{"text":"SUMIFS"},{"text":"COUNTIFS"},{"text":"XLOOKUP"},{"text":"INDEX/MATCH"},{"text":"Text functions"},{"text":"Date functions"},{"text":"Pivot Tables"},{"text":"Pivot Charts"},{"text":"Conditional formatting"},{"text":"Charts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Excel"},{"type":"p","text":"Progress to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Power Pivot"},{"text":"Data modelling"},{"text":"Dynamic arrays"},{"text":"Scenario analysis"},{"text":"Forecasting"},{"text":"A good analyst should be able to take a messy spreadsheet and produce a clean analytical output."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"SQL should become a core professional skill."},{"type":"h","text":"Fundamentals"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SELECT"},{"text":"FROM"},{"text":"WHERE"},{"text":"ORDER BY"},{"text":"GROUP BY"},{"text":"HAVING"},{"text":"DISTINCT"},{"text":"CASE"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"INNER JOIN"},{"text":"LEFT JOIN"},{"text":"RIGHT JOIN"},{"text":"UNION"},{"text":"Subqueries"},{"text":"CTEs"},{"text":"Window Functions"},{"text":"Date Functions"},{"text":"Aggregations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced SQL"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ranking"},{"text":"Running totals"},{"text":"Moving averages"},{"text":"Cohort calculations"},{"text":"Percentages"},{"text":"Segmentation"},{"text":"Time-based comparisons"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Example"},{"type":"flow","items":["Business Database","SQL","Filter","Join","Aggregate","Calculate KPIs","Analyse Trends","Business Insight"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3 — Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Python transforms the Mathematics background into a scalable analytical skill."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Data types"},{"text":"Conditions"},{"text":"Loops"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Lists"},{"text":"Dictionaries"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"Exceptions"},{"text":"Modules"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Then focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"Matplotlib"},{"text":"Seaborn"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"Jupyter"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python for Data Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"pandas"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"DataFrames"},{"text":"Filtering"},{"text":"Sorting"},{"text":"GroupBy"},{"text":"Aggregation"},{"text":"Merge"},{"text":"Join"},{"text":"Pivot"},{"text":"Reshape"},{"text":"Missing values"},{"text":"Duplicate removal"},{"text":"Date/time operations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["CSV / Database","Python","pandas","Data Cleaning","EDA","Statistical Analysis","Visualization","Insights"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2–3 — Applied Statistics"},{"type":"p","text":"This should become the strongest competitive advantage of the Mathematics graduate."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn deeply"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Sampling theory"},{"text":"Estimation"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"t-tests"},{"text":"Chi-square tests"},{"text":"ANOVA"},{"text":"Correlation"},{"text":"Linear regression"},{"text":"Multiple regression"},{"text":"Statistical significance"},{"text":"Effect size"},{"text":"Statistical power"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Important principle"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not just calculate a p-value."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn to determine:"},{"type":"p","text":"Is the result statistically meaningful, practically important, and supported by an appropriate experimental design?"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Data Visualization"},{"type":"p","text":"A mathematically correct analysis is not useful if decision-makers cannot understand it."},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Tableau"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Python"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Power BI"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Power Query"},{"text":"Data modelling"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"DAX"},{"text":"Measures"},{"text":"Calculated columns"},{"text":"KPI cards"},{"text":"Slicers"},{"text":"Drill-through"},{"text":"Interactive reports"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Visualization principles"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to choose:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Line charts"},{"text":"Bar charts"},{"text":"Scatter plots"},{"text":"Histograms"},{"text":"Box plots"},{"text":"Heatmaps"},{"text":"Maps"},{"text":"based on the analytical question."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Exploratory Data Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop a repeatable EDA framework."},{"type":"flow","items":["Dataset","Understand Variables","Data Quality","Missing Values","Outliers","Distributions","Relationships","Segmentation","Trends","Anomalies","Insights"]},{"type":"h","text":"Questions to ask"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What happened?"},{"text":"When did it happen?"},{"text":"Where did it happen?"},{"text":"Which segment changed?"},{"text":"What variables are related?"},{"text":"Is the relationship meaningful?"},{"text":"What could explain the pattern?"},{"text":"What action should follow?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4 — Business Analytics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"This is the major transition from Mathematics graduate → professional Data Analyst."},{"text":"Learn the language of business."}]